## Known landmines / Do-not-repeat
A short, scannable list of hazards: the things that broke the machine, corrupted a run, or cost
hours. Distinct from the ED rationale below, this is the fast pre-flight checklist. Re-check it before any
action matching a listed trigger (GPU use, launching a detached/long process, overwriting inputs, …).
Before complying with a request that would hit a listed landmine, surface that landmine to the user; do
not walk into it silently. A landmine recorded only in a chat message or a memory file is not re-checked,
and the hazard recurs. Record it in this table.

| trigger (when about to…) | landmine (what went wrong) | do instead |
|---|---|---|
| <e.g. use the GPU for the dictionary build> | <froze the machine; hard reboot> | <use the CPU-parallel path; do not re-enable the GPU build> |

